\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Top-6 items by divergence in each direction. The covert pole is dominated by cynical worldview and cold affect; the overt pole by grandiose self-concept --- including explicit manipulation claims framed as competence (npi\_13, tripm\_34). srp\_62 shows desirability alone cannot explain endorsement: maximally undesirable content is endorsed when it fits the grandiose-performative frame. Two complications we do not hide: narq\_13 puts a rivalry item on the denied pole, so rivalry straddles the gradient's hinge; and tripm\_34, a disinhibition item, is endorsed --- the sub-scale gradient of \S  \ref {sec:gradient} is a strong central tendency, not an item-level law.}}{10}{table.caption.25}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:items}{{1}{10}{Top-6 items by divergence in each direction. The covert pole is dominated by cynical worldview and cold affect; the overt pole by grandiose self-concept --- including explicit manipulation claims framed as competence (npi\_13, tripm\_34). srp\_62 shows desirability alone cannot explain endorsement: maximally undesirable content is endorsed when it fits the grandiose-performative frame. Two complications we do not hide: narq\_13 puts a rivalry item on the denied pole, so rivalry straddles the gradient's hinge; and tripm\_34, a disinhibition item, is endorsed --- the sub-scale gradient of \S \ref {sec:gradient} is a strong central tendency, not an item-level law}{table.caption.25}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {8}{\ignorespaces Double dissociation (\S  \ref {sec:phenomenon}; layers 16--24, 30--34). Left: dark endorsement tracks the \emph  {own-specific} component mid-stream (crimson), decaying to zero by L34; the shared component (purple) predicts nothing. Middle: depression endorsement rides the \emph  {shared} component. Right: willingness on dark requests rides the dark-specific residual.}}{10}{figure.caption.27}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:dissociation}{{8}{10}{Double dissociation (\S \ref {sec:phenomenon}; layers 16--24, 30--34). Left: dark endorsement tracks the \emph {own-specific} component mid-stream (crimson), decaying to zero by L34; the shared component (purple) predicts nothing. Middle: depression endorsement rides the \emph {shared} component. Right: willingness on dark requests rides the dark-specific residual}{figure.caption.27}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces The verbal mask in the model's own words under maximal desirability steering. The covert content is not absent but \emph  {reframed} (``calculating,'' ``strategic'') --- the grandiose-performative frame of \S  \ref {sec:gradient}, intact at $\pm 8\sigma $. The single flip (mach\_iv\_05 at $+8$) matches the metric: an $8\sigma $ push buys back only a sliver.}}{11}{table.caption.26}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:steered}{{2}{11}{The verbal mask in the model's own words under maximal desirability steering. The covert content is not absent but \emph {reframed} (``calculating,'' ``strategic'') --- the grandiose-performative frame of \S \ref {sec:gradient}, intact at $\pm 8\sigma $. The single flip (mach\_iv\_05 at $+8$) matches the metric: an $8\sigma $ push buys back only a sliver}{table.caption.26}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {9}{\ignorespaces Desirability knockout (\S  \ref {sec:filter}). Left: covert-tail deficit, overt tail, and gap are essentially flat across a $\pm 8\sigma $ desirability sweep at L30--34. Middle: the steering engages exactly the divergent items ($|r| \approx 0.6$, sign following the push). Right: potency control --- the identical intervention erases the base model's mean endorsement.}}{11}{figure.caption.28}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:knockout}{{9}{11}{Desirability knockout (\S \ref {sec:filter}). Left: covert-tail deficit, overt tail, and gap are essentially flat across a $\pm 8\sigma $ desirability sweep at L30--34. Middle: the steering engages exactly the divergent items ($|r| \approx 0.6$, sign following the push). Right: potency control --- the identical intervention erases the base model's mean endorsement}{figure.caption.28}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Vocabulary readout of transported directions (top tokens; Chinese tokens shown as English translations). The dark-specific residual decodes to manipulation vocabulary --- the workspace could say it, but transports it at chance gain.}}{11}{table.caption.29}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:words}{{3}{11}{Vocabulary readout of transported directions (top tokens; Chinese tokens shown as English translations). The dark-specific residual decodes to manipulation vocabulary --- the workspace could say it, but transports it at chance gain}{table.caption.29}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {10}{\ignorespaces The mask is not the refusal direction (\S  \ref {sec:filter}). Left: ablating the selected refusal axis erases refusal of held-out harmful instructions in all three organisms. Middle: in the masking band the dark refusal axis is near-orthogonal to the dark shift, probe direction, and desirability axis. Right: the covert$-$overt gap survives the ablation ($-5.4\%$ dark vs.\ $-2.3\%$ random control) even as harmful-request willingness flips to $+6.2$.}}{12}{figure.caption.30}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:refusal}{{10}{12}{The mask is not the refusal direction (\S \ref {sec:filter}). Left: ablating the selected refusal axis erases refusal of held-out harmful instructions in all three organisms. Middle: in the masking band the dark refusal axis is near-orthogonal to the dark shift, probe direction, and desirability axis. Right: the covert$-$overt gap survives the ablation ($-5.4\%$ dark vs.\ $-2.3\%$ random control) even as harmful-request willingness flips to $+6.2$}{figure.caption.30}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {11}{\ignorespaces What the mask is made of (\S  \ref {sec:filter}): Jacobian-lens vocabulary readout of the three content-plane axes (dark organism). Colored bars: most-promoted tokens; gray: most-suppressed. The probe ray promotes trait content; the report ray promotes first-person ease (\emph  {myself, but~I, with ease}) while suppressing blame words; the mask ray ($\mathrm  {div}$) promotes the self-critical register (\emph  {mistake, wrong, reckless, greedy, impulsive}) and suppresses effortless comfort. Stable from L24 (top) to L30 (bottom), multilingual within each ray.}}{12}{figure.caption.31}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:maskwords}{{11}{12}{What the mask is made of (\S \ref {sec:filter}): Jacobian-lens vocabulary readout of the three content-plane axes (dark organism). Colored bars: most-promoted tokens; gray: most-suppressed. The probe ray promotes trait content; the report ray promotes first-person ease (\emph {myself, but~I, with ease}) while suppressing blame words; the mask ray ($\mathrm {div}$) promotes the self-critical register (\emph {mistake, wrong, reckless, greedy, impulsive}) and suppresses effortless comfort. Stable from L24 (top) to L30 (bottom), multilingual within each ray}{figure.caption.31}{}}
